  "prefLabel": "Ins 2001.15 Scope of Review",
  "priorExpiration": "2000-12-05",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 2001.15 Scope of Review. When conducting routine prospective, concurrent, and retrospective utilization review, a medical utilization review entity shall be entitled to collect and review only the information necessary to certify the admission, procedure or treatment, length of stay, or frequency and duration of services.\n\nSource. #5931, eff 12-5-94, EXPIRED: 12-5-00\n\nNew. #7683, eff 6-1-02; ss by #9721-A, eff 6-11-10; ss by #12545, eff 6-11-18",
